course: dictionary
lesson: 5154
title: Iroquoian: a family of languages
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Iroquoian is a word for a family of languages, a bit like how a family shares a surname. The languages are spoken by Native American and First Nations peoples of north-eastern North America. «The name Canada comes from kanata, an Iroquoian word for village that Cartier heard.» The context tells you that kanata is a word from one of these languages.
explain: Read the words around Iroquoian to find its job. In «Iroquoian languages», it describes the languages. In «Iroquoian peoples», it describes the people. Ask yourself: what does this word describe? Then swap in a simple meaning, such as "the languages of the Iroquoian family", to see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Iroquoian is a family of languages spoken by Native American and First Nations peoples of north-eastern North America.
fact: Mohawk, Seneca, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga, Tuscarora and Cherokee are all Iroquoian languages.
fact: «Iroquoian peoples» lived around the Great Lakes and St Lawrence River, often in longhouses.
fact: Iroquoian peoples grew the «Three Sisters»: corn, beans and squash.
fact: «Iroquoian» can also describe the peoples, their languages and their culture.
exercise: What is Iroquoian? | A river in Canada | *A family of languages spoken in north-eastern North America | A food made from corn | A kind of longhouse
exercise: «The name Canada comes from kanata, an Iroquoian word for village.» What does Iroquoian tell you about kanata? | *It is a word from an Iroquoian language | It is a name for a river | It is a British word | It is a type of corn
exercise: Which of these is an Iroquoian language? | Spanish | Japanese | French | *Mohawk
test: Which crops made up the «Three Sisters»? | Rice, wheat and oats | Apples, pears and plums | *Corn, beans and squash | Potatoes, carrots and onions
test: Where did many Iroquoian peoples live? | In the deserts of Arabia | *Around the Great Lakes and St Lawrence River | In the Australian outback | On the Himalayan mountains
exam: Which phrase uses Iroquoian to describe people? | Iroquoian sea | Iroquoian sky | Iroquoian bread | *Iroquoian peoples
